    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Gunnar Henderson** (62.61) and **Heliot Ramos** (61.69) represent our strongest offensive engines. **Gunnar Henderson** benefits significantly from hitting in the two-hole against a vulnerable starter, and his score receives a subtle lift from a favorable stolen base environment created by Weathers' slow delivery. Meanwhile, **Heliot Ramos** is our primary target for efficiency; his matchup against Sasaki is the most favorable of the day, as he avoids elite pitching and benefits from a generous SP_xERA of 5.30. While **Coby Mayo** (59.21) also draws a decent matchup, the core of our production relies on **Gunnar Henderson** setting the table and **Heliot Ramos** capitalizing on a weak starter to drive up our counting stats in a category-constrained 5x5 environment.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Josh Jung**, whose 46.79 score kept him in the conversation until the final verification. Ultimately, the optimizer prioritized the higher floor of **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (55.86) and the specific category requirements we face; while **Josh Jung** is a viable rotation piece, his matchup against Soroka lacked the dynamic upside required to displace our current starters. We are monitoring the risk surrounding **Andy Pages** (42.81) and **Kyle Tucker** (53.64), both of whom are facing the toughest matchup of the day against McDonald (2.60 xERA). Given the elite nature of that opposing arm, their scoring output is suppressed; however, they remain locked in to provide exposure to high-leverage at-bats. We continue to manage our bench depth\u2014including **Jackson Merrill**, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, and **Luis Robert Jr.**\u2014as we await recovery timelines and lineup clarity for the coming week.",
